  "notes": "The C engine does not emit a GL call stream (SPEC: GL is the numerical oracle), so the shader and FBO wrappers are recorded n/a rather than missing. The behavioral members are glBlendFunc and setLightmapTextureCoords, mirrored by the entity_raster_target fields in csrc/engine/raster_entity_quad.h and cited in comments across raster_entities.c, raster_worldfx.c and raster_hud.c. Not gaps (triage 2026-09-25, out/plan/remaining-2026-09-25.md): GL plumbing: GL is the numerical oracle, not emitted (SPEC); atlases and meshes are consumed as data. Formerly listed as missing: The fixed-function separate blend (glBlendFunc's four factors) exists only as the raster target's coarse blend modes; any caller using factor combinations outside those modes would render differently."
